Z||000004||Nashco||11-23-2001||12:48 PM||||You know, I'd love to hear more on crash safety too.  I've seen bits and pieces of crash stuff, but I never bookmarked any of it because I didn't care.  I have a friend who really likes them, but worries they're not safe enough (he has kids, can't blame in that situation).  I have explained the space frame, and how you're literally inside of a cage that has huge crumple zones (especially up front).  I also told him about the heavy cross bars in the door that most racers take out, they're that heavy.  He has a Saturn, which uses almost all of the same safety measures and rated very high for compact car crash tests, so he understands the concept, just has a hard time believing the Fiero was that far ahead in crash safety.<P>So, who has some links they could post?  Oh, by the way, your link didn't work REDHOTT88.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
